    },
    {
      "claim": "Poor solubility is common in this chemotype, for example vismodegib 1 µg/mL at pH 7, DNDI-VL-2098 about 10 µM, and regorafenib below 0.1 mg/mL, but solubility limitation alone is not affirmative evidence for F below 20% because esaxerenone with Fa at least 80% and nilotinib with F 31% show high lipophilicity does not preclude the threshold.",
      "card_ids": ["C103", "C148", "C110", "C131", "C06"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "No L4 record provides a direct F below 20% outcome for the query or a close analog; high efflux ratios in some analogs are context and not threshold-relevant proof of low oral bioavailability.",
