  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement for the query molecule.",
    "No query-specific solubility or permeability data; L4 evidence is analog-based.",
    "No gut-wall efflux or intestinal metabolism data for the query; L5 not yet assessed.",
    "Aqueous solubility of the query at gastrointestinal pH is unknown and the high logD of 5.82 remains a risk, not proof of low F.",
    "No dose, formulation, or food-effect data for the query, so dissolution-limited absorption cannot be quantified."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Keep high prediction and strengthen the decision. L4 adds affirmative absorption evidence: esaxerenone has a human absorption fraction of at least 80% and high Caco-2 permeability, and several OCF3 or CF3 lipophilic amide analogs show high permeability. Solubility concerns remain but are not affirmative evidence for F below 20%, and no L4 record provides a transferable direct low-F outcome. Confidence stays moderate because query-specific experimental data are absent."
